description:
OBJECTIVE: Turn build timing and cache behavior into structured facts, not shell archaeology.

DATA MODEL every build emits:
{
  release_unit_id: <source_sha>,
  workflow_run_id: ...,
  job_name: 'Build OpenEdX Image',
  runner_class: 'fastlane|arc-heavy|arc-standard',
  queue_seconds: ...,
  build_seconds: ...,
  scan_seconds: ...,
  cache_sources: [{type: 'registry', ref: '...', hit: true/false}],
  cache_export: {type: 'registry', ref: '...', success: true/false},
  image_digest: 'sha256:...'
}

METRICS TO STANDARDIZE:
- ci_queue_duration_seconds
- ci_build_duration_seconds{image=openedx|mfe}
- ci_scan_duration_seconds{tool=syft|trivy,image=...}
- ci_cache_source_found{image,source=registry|image|gha|local}
- ci_cache_export_succeeded{image,source=registry}
- ci_layer_reuse_ratio{image}
- ci_failure_total{class=source|workflow|runner|platform}
- ci_release_unit_info{source_sha,...}

EXISTING: emit-build-metrics.sh (delivered in PR #1779) parses buildx metadata. BUT no receiver ingests it yet. Data goes to workflow artifact only.

DOD: We can answer 'why was this build slow?' with metrics, not anecdotes.
